#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The HypeLLM reference job shim.

A job shim stands beside one generative service and speaks the router's job
protocol on its behalf (orchestration §11.3). This one is the reference: it
serves the protocol for any service that can be run as a command, and it is
what a service-specific shim is measured against. It is **not** part of the
HypeLLM workspace and is not built by `cargo build --workspace`, for the same
reason `agent/` and `tls-helper/` are not: the router never executes a process
(specification 26.2), and running a generator is exactly that.

    GET    /job/v1/health                 → 200 { verbs[] }
    POST   /job/v1/jobs                   → 202 { id }
    GET    /job/v1/jobs/{id}              → { state, progress_permille, eta_ms, elapsed_ms, error, parts[] }
    GET    /job/v1/jobs/{id}/parts/{name} → bytes, with Content-Type and Content-Length
    DELETE /job/v1/jobs/{id}              → 202 { stopped }

The rules it exists to keep
---------------------------

1. **The router authenticates, every request.** A bearer token from a key file,
   compared in constant time. Nothing — not health — answers without it. Run
   the service itself where only this shim can reach it.
2. **Inputs are bytes, never references.** An input is a name, a media type
   from a closed set, and base64 data. There is no field for a URL or a path,
   so a caller cannot make the service read a file or fetch a host; inputs are
   written into the job's own directory under names this shim chooses.
3. **No shell.** A verb runs a configured argv — an absolute program and fixed
   arguments — with placeholders replaced by whole values. The prompt is one
   argument, passed literally; `; rm -rf /` in a prompt is a prompt.
4. **Outputs are declared.** A verb lists the files it produces and their media
   types. After the command exits, each must be a regular file — not a link —
   inside the job's output directory, within the size cap. Anything else fails
   the job; nothing undeclared is ever served.
5. **Closed vocabularies.** States, error codes and media types are the
   protocol's own sets. A command signals `invalid_input` by exiting 65
   (EX_DATAERR) and `out_of_memory` by exiting 75 (EX_TEMPFAIL); any other
   failure is `internal`.
6. **Everything is bounded.** Request bodies, inputs, concurrent connections,
   one job running at a time, a job's wall time, retained jobs, and part
   sizes. A job's directory is removed when it is cancelled or expires.
7. **No prompt is logged.** A log line names the method, the route and the
   status, never a body.

Configuration is a JSON file; see `job-shim.example.json` beside this file and
spec/components/job-shim.html.
"""

